course: dictionary
lesson: 14351
title: Olden times
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Olden is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you that something belongs to the long-ago past. «In the olden days, children walked to school because there were no cars.» The phrase tells you the time is far back, so olden means long ago.
explain: You will mostly hear olden in two phrases: «in the olden days» and «olden times». Both mean a long time ago. Grandparents often use them when they talk about life before phones, cars or electricity.
explain: Olden is not the same as old. A phone that is three years old is old, but it is not olden. Olden points to a whole time far back in the past.
fact: Olden means belonging to the long-ago past.
fact: «In the olden days» means a long time ago.
fact: «Olden times» means the same as the long-ago past.
fact: Olden goes before a noun, like «olden days» or «olden times».
fact: In history lessons you could say «in the past» instead, which means the same thing.
exercise: «In the olden days, people wrote letters by hand and sent them by post.» What does olden mean here? | Very loud | *Belonging to the long-ago past | Far away across the sea | Brand new and shiny
exercise: Grandma says, «When I was small, we had no mobile phones in olden times.» What does olden times mean? | This very morning | Tomorrow | During the summer holidays | *A long time ago
exercise: Which phrase means a long time ago? | in the sunny days | in the busy days | *in the olden days | in the new days
test: «Olden toys were made of wood and tin, long before plastic was used.» What does olden mean? | Very expensive | Brand new | Made of plastic | *Long ago in the past
test: Which sentence uses olden correctly? | *The museum shows clothes that people wore in olden times | The shop sells olden trainers that were bought yesterday | My olden lunch is in my bag this morning | Olden is the cat sleeping on the sofa
exam: Ali says, «The olden castle is closed on Mondays.» Is Ali's use of olden correct? | *Yes, a castle from long ago can be called olden | No, olden means closed | No, olden only describes people, never places | No, castles are never old enough to be olden
